<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding a translation vector</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A translation maps \(P({@p1@},\,{@p2@})\) to \(P'({@Pi[1]@},\,{@Pi[2]@})\).</p><p>(a) Find the translation vector \(\mathbf{T}\).</p><div>\(\mathbf{T} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The same translation maps a point Q to \(Q'({@q1i@},\,{@q2i@})\). Find Q.</p><div>Q = ( [[input:ans2]] , [[input:ans3]] ) [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]]</div><div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(\mathbf{T}\) is the move from P to P': image minus object. Across: \([[if test="is(p1<0)"]]{@Pi[1]@} - ({@p1@})[[else]]{@Pi[1]@} - {@p1@}[[/if]] = {@t1@}\); up: \([[if test="is(p2<0)"]]{@Pi[2]@} - ({@p2@})[[else]]{@Pi[2]@} - {@p2@}[[/if]] = {@t2@}\). So \(\mathbf{T} = {@tT@}\).</p><p>(b) Q' is the image, so go back: \(Q = Q' - \mathbf{T}\). Across: \([[if test="is(t1<0)"]]{@q1i@} - ({@t1@})[[else]]{@q1i@} - {@t1@}[[/if]] = {@Q[1]@}\); up: \([[if test="is(t2<0)"]]{@q2i@} - ({@t2@})[[else]]{@q2i@} - {@t2@}[[/if]] = {@Q[2]@}\). So \(Q({@Q[1]@},\,{@Q[2]@})\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
col(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]]);
/* Design: the column vector of a given translation, by coordinates, with the reverse step added. Source: adapted from SMP GCSE Foundation 2, Chapter 15, Section B, B7. */
p1: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]); t1: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]); t2: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);
p2: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0, if p1=-2*t1 then -2*t2 else 0]);
q1i: rand(11)-5; q2i: rand(11)-5;
P: [p1,p2]; T: [t1,t2]; Pi: P+T; Qi: [q1i,q2i]; Q: Qi-T;
tT: col(T); trev: col(P-Pi); tPi: col(Pi);
tw1: tT+matrix([1],[0]); badm: matrix([q],[1]);
fw: Qi+T; ftq: Qi-T-[1,0];
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
